  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${\u222c}_{D}xy\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}xy\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y(\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
